# {{ project_name }}

Install uv, Node 24, pnpm and Go Task.

```sh
task setup
{% if enable_jobs %}
task jobs:redis
# Separate terminal: task jobs:worker
{% endif %}
task dev
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:5173. API health: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health.

Official shadcn-svelte components are vendored in frontend/src/lib/components/ui. Use the registry CLI only when adding new components. Commit uv/pnpm lockfiles after setup.

## Production and tailnet

Install Caddy, run task build and task serve from the project directory. Caddy binds to loopback on port 8080. For private HTTPS access, authenticate Tailscale, enable MagicDNS and HTTPS, then run task tailscale. Restrict tailnet grants to intended users/devices. Do not use Funnel without introducing application authentication. For direct LAN access explicitly configure a Caddy listener, HTTPS and appropriate access controls.

MCP: streamable HTTP at /mcp/ on the API or Caddy origin; exposes read-only list_notes. Native browser notifications require permission and localhost or HTTPS. They work while the page is open; no background push service is included.
{% if enable_terminal %}

## Terminal

Install ttyd (includes xterm.js) on the Linux host. Run as an unprivileged account. Create a strong password hash using caddy hash-password and export it as TERMINAL_PASSWORD_HASH in Caddy's process environment. Run task terminal separately. Caddy protects terminal HTTP and WebSocket routes with basic authentication (username operator). Open through Caddy, not Vite. Do not expose ttyd directly; a shell has the privileges of the host account.
{% endif %}

## Development

task check, task fix, task test, task test:e2e, task build. Install Chromium using cd frontend && pnpm exec playwright install chromium (then return to the project root). After git init, install hooks using uv run pre-commit install.


## Reusable UI

SvelteKit is configured as a static SPA (SSR disabled), solely for supported Formsnap/Superforms integration. FastAPI remains the sole application backend. Build output remains frontend/dist. The example notes screen includes TanStack sorting, filtering, pagination, PaneForge resizable/persistent layout, and Zod/Formsnap validation. The diagnostics screen uses psutil host and process metrics.
{% if enable_events %}

## Live updates

The optional /api/events SSE stream sends current notes on connection and when the database changes, including changes made by another process such as a Taskiq worker. EventSource reconnects automatically. The browser displays a toast and, if granted permission, a native notification. The starter polls SQLite once per second per connected client; it does not provide durable event history or push while the page is closed.
{% endif %}

## Screenshots

Run task screenshots after installing Chromium. The Playwright capture suite saves real PNGs in screenshots/ using a dedicated test database. The source template has a manual Screenshots workflow to publish images.
